From: Project Luma
Subject: [PATCH] theme: frost and glass title rows are light, with dark ink

Owner, 2026-09-18: frost and glass had turned into dark mode. 0038 gave their
title rows a smoked veil with white ink, and the kit tokens smoked every
window surface the same way, so a Frost or Glass window read as Dark. Frost
and glass are light, see-through panels over the wallpaper, as the thumbnails
in Settings > Appearance show.

The title row keeps a veil, because a title drawn straight on the see-through
frame measured 1.54:1 on glass over a dark wallpaper, but the veil is a light
one: rgba(251,251,250,.92) on frost and rgba(246,244,240,.88) on glass, with
the light family's dark ink. Composited over black, the worst case, a title
measures 10.8:1 on frost and 8.8:1 on glass, so the white ink and its drop
shadow are not needed and are removed. The checked-control fills on the title
row take the frost and glass state slate (#56667c with white, 3:1 or better
from the veil). The tiled-window stroke from 0038 is unchanged.

Every Luma title row is drawn on the window frame, which on glass is
see-through at .31; there Settings' title measured 2.8:1 over the default blue
wallpaper. On frost and glass the frame now carries the title-row veil
(@luma_chrome) as a 42px band behind the title row, the lighter band the
thumbnails show. It is drawn by the window itself, so kit windows, native
windows and Filer all get it.

Dimmed text (row subtitles, captions, .dim-label) moves from the stock 55%
of the ink to 78%, in every mode: 55% measured 3.4:1 for the Reduce
Transparency subtitle, and 78% holds 4.5:1 on every Luma surface, a glass
island over black included (4.52:1). High
contrast keeps 90%.
---
diff --git a/src/stylesheet/widgets/_header-bar.scss b/src/stylesheet/widgets/_header-bar.scss
index 255da36..e3b9581 100644
--- a/src/stylesheet/widgets/_header-bar.scss
+++ b/src/stylesheet/widgets/_header-bar.scss
@@ -667,3 +667,83 @@ headerbar.luma-command-host {
     margin: 0 4px;
   }
 }
+
+// Frost and glass title rows are light, like the panels under them and the
+// thumbnails in Settings > Appearance: a denser light veil than the window
+// frame, carrying the light family's dark ink. The veil is what keeps a
+// title at 4.5:1 or better over any wallpaper, black included (glass 8.8:1,
+// frost 10.8:1 for the title; 4.5:1 for the quietest text), so neither the
+// white ink nor its shadow is needed. This replaces the smoked veil of 0038
+// and the smoked-header control fills of 0039; the tiled-window stroke stays.
+window.csd.luma-treatment-frost {
+  --headerbar-bg-color: rgba(251, 251, 250, 0.92);
+  --headerbar-fg-color: #283038;
+}
+
+window.csd.luma-treatment-glass {
+  --headerbar-bg-color: rgba(246, 244, 240, 0.88);
+  --headerbar-fg-color: #2c343a;
+}
+
+window.csd.luma-treatment-frost headerbar,
+window.csd.luma-treatment-glass headerbar {
+  --luma-state: #56667c;
+  --luma-state-ink: #ffffff;
+  --luma-knob: #ffffff;
+  --luma-knob-ring: #56667c;
+}
+
+window.csd.luma-treatment-frost windowtitle .title,
+window.csd.luma-treatment-glass windowtitle .title,
+window.csd.luma-treatment-frost headerbar .luma-identity-button > button,
+window.csd.luma-treatment-glass headerbar .luma-identity-button > button {
+  text-shadow: none;
+}
+
+window.csd.luma-treatment-frost headerbar windowcontrols button > image,
+window.csd.luma-treatment-glass headerbar windowcontrols button > image,
+window.csd.luma-treatment-frost headerbar .luma-identity-icon,
+window.csd.luma-treatment-glass headerbar .luma-identity-icon,
+window.csd.luma-treatment-frost headerbar .luma-identity-chevron,
+window.csd.luma-treatment-glass headerbar .luma-identity-chevron {
+  -gtk-icon-shadow: none;
+}
+
+@media (prefers-contrast: more) {
+  window.csd.luma-treatment-frost headerbar,
+  window.csd.luma-treatment-glass headerbar {
+    box-shadow: inset 0 -1px rgba(37, 46, 54, 0.30);
+  }
+}
+
+// Every Luma title row is drawn on the window frame (a kit window's top bar
+// and a native window's headerbar both leave it showing), and the glass frame
+// is see-through at .31: Settings' title measured 2.8:1 over the default blue
+// wallpaper and 1.5:1 over black. On frost and glass the frame carries the
+// title-row veil (@luma_chrome: .92 frost, .88 glass) behind the 42px title
+// row, the lighter band the Appearance thumbnails show, so a title holds
+// 4.5:1 or better over any wallpaper. Light and dark keep one continuous frame.
+window.luma-treatment-frost,
+window.luma-treatment-glass,
+window.luma-treatment-frost:backdrop,
+window.luma-treatment-glass:backdrop {
+  background-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, unquote("@luma_chrome"), unquote("@luma_chrome"));
+  background-size: 100% 42px;
+  background-position: top;
+  background-repeat: no-repeat;
+}
+
+// Dimmed text (row subtitles, captions, .dim-label) is the ink at
+// --dim-opacity. Stock 55% gives about 3.8:1 on paper and less on a frost or
+// glass island over a dark wallpaper; 78% holds 4.5:1 or better on every Luma
+// surface in all four modes (Settings > Appearance's Reduce Transparency
+// subtitle measured 3.4:1 before). High contrast keeps its own 90%.
+:root {
+  --dim-opacity: 78%;
+}
+
+@media (prefers-contrast: more) {
+  :root {
+    --dim-opacity: 90%;
+  }
+}
